$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
compound 10a, 10d-10j, 10l-10p, 10s-10u: A mixture of 4 (1.0 equiv, each
one), amine (1.5~2 equiv), HATU (1.2 equiv) and DIPEA (2.0 equiv) in dry
DCM (2~5 mL) was stirred for 8 to 10 h at room temperature. Then the
reaction mixture was diluted with DCM (15 mL), washed with water (10
mL*2) and brine (10 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by prep-HPLC. 10a,
10d-10j, 10l-10p, 10s-10u in 9-80% yield, respectively. Compound 10c:
Yield: 41 mg, 72%. Positive ESIMS [M + Na]+ m/z 592; 1H NMR (600 MHz,
CDCl3) δ H: 6.97 (2H, t, J = 8.6 Hz, H-2' and H-6'), 6.82 (2H, t, J = 8.6
Hz, H-3' and H-5'), 4.52 (1H, s, H-18a), 4.49 (1H, s, H-18b), 4.03 (1H,
d, J = 11.5 Hz), 3.80-3.44 (10H, overlapped), 3.76 (3H, s, OMe), 2.85
(1H, d, J = 10.0 Hz), 2.30-1.84 (6H, overlapped), 1.60-1.17 (8H,
overlapped), 1.04 (3H, s, H3-19), 0.97 (3H, s, H3-20), 0.91 (3H, s,
H3-16), 0.81 (3H, d, J = 6.7 Hz, H3-17); 13C NMR (151 MHz, CDCl3) δ C:
171.9, 169.5, 160.4, 158.5, 130.7, 128.3, 113.9, 103.0, 85.0, 66.6, 66.1,
55.4, 50.4, 48.8, 45.8, 44.4, 42.8, 42.6, 40.4, 39.9, 39.8, 39.1, 37.0,
37.0, 33.2, 28.5, 27.9, 23.6, 22.8, 20.7, 16.8, 13.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
